      "role": "user",
      "content": "cool. here is the report content. try to keep it concise but very data-heavy.\n\n[Market Intelligence Report Q3 - Sector Analysis]\n\nThe fintech sector saw a significant shift this quarter. Total venture capital inflow into fintech decreased from $12.4 billion in Q2 to $9.8 billion in Q3, representing a 20.9% decline. Despite this, Neobanking remains a resilient sub-sector, capturing 15% of the total fintech investment pool. \n\nIn the E-commerce space, growth has stabilized. Average transaction values rose by 4.2% compared to last year, while user acquisition costs (CAC) increased by 11.5%, putting pressure on margins for smaller players. \n\nRenewable energy investments spiked, with a 33% YoY increase in Series A funding. Specifically, solar tech saw a 22% rise, while wind energy stagnated at 2% growth. \n\nLastly, the AI/ML landscape continues to dominate. 45% of all new VC deals in Q3 were related to generative AI applications, up from 28% in Q1. The median deal size for AI startups has reached $18.5 million, a substantial jump from the $12.2 million seen in previous years.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
